{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["Then Esav despised — because in the end he regretted it, as written: את בכורתי לקח. Therefore he anticipated here, to inform us of his folly at this moment: on account of eating he despised the birthright, but in the end he came to regret it." "ויבז — like ויבזה from 'despising a thing of YHWH he despised,' just as: ויקן from קנה."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "The lemma in the first example is from Proverbs (the supplied clause is from the conventional phrasing); Rashbam illustrates the elision of the heh from the cardinal form by analogy with a similar morphological elision."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:15.412726528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}